      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In both cases, don't you set the nearClipPlane value of the reference camera and then put the reference camera into the VRCWorld component? Basically all my worlds, SDK2 or 3, has the nearclip plane at 0.01\nThat said, this is *not* the actual limit. Changing it to anything smaller will make Unity change it back, but by using custom scripts you can force it smaller. I tried an editor script and got it to 0.001, but uploading it like that changed it back to 0.01 (so I probably didn't do it properly)\nI tried freezing it at 0.001 with Cheat Engine and uploading the world, but that crashed everything. If somebody who knows a bit about how Unity works would make a script which freezes the near clip plane before the world is build, I'd really like to have it. (You could even sell it on booth!)\nPS: With a low near-clipping-plane you will run into Z-fighting problems in larger worlds.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
