      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f5fc0d21be0a243b0ffe6af|full_name}: On the default camera, you can't make it go below 0.03? It should change to 0.01 if you try to make it lower.\nI have succeeded in making it less than 0.01 with an editor script in Unity, just not in VRChat. This is because it overwrites it *after* my script is run, or because my script changes it *after* it's done building (I'm not really sure which)\nI've made a shader to read the nearclipplane of worlds, and most are 0.01 or they have no setting of their own (in which case it will use the reference camera of the previous world). The player camera is usually 0.03 though. There's a way to change that camera too, but I have no idea how.\nVRC devs can probably figure it out if enough players want it (maybe add it as a room mod like walk speed?) but Udon seemingly doesn't have any runtime access to the players camera, so I doubt we can do much about it ourselves.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-09-16T15:09:48.359Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In SDK2, there seemed to be no limit on what you could set the reference camera's near clipping plane to, but in SDK3 it seems this is limited to between 0.03 and 0.05. It would be good to either expand this range or remove the limitation entirely. I'd like to make my worlds small-avatar-friendly, but unfortunately I can't due to this limitation.\nThere are some similar posts relating to clipping plane configuration, but none specifically about SDK3:\n- https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/adjust-avatar-camera-near-clip-plane\n- https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/adjustable-camera-clipping\n- https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/allow-the-camera-near-clip-plane-to-be-configured-by-the-player\nI've attached some screenshots for reference. Thank you for considering!",
